#: source/language/identifiers.md:1
msgid "Identifiers"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:3
msgid ""
"An _identifier_ is an [ASCII](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ASCII) character "
"sequence that:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:4
msgid "Starts with a letter (`a-z`, `A-Z`) or underscore (`_`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:5
msgid "Can contain any number of:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:6
msgid "Letters (`a-z`, `A-Z`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:7
msgid "Digits (`0-9`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:8
msgid "Underscores (`_`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:9
msgid "Apostrophes (`'`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:10
msgid "Hyphens (`-`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:11
msgid "Is not one of the [keywords](#keywords)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:13 source/language/identifiers.md:21
msgid "**Syntax**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:15
msgid "_identifier_ ~ `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_'-]*`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:17
msgid "Names"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:19
msgid ""
"A _name_ can be written as an [identifier](#identifiers) or a [string "
"literal](./string-literals.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:23
msgid "_name_ → _identifier_ | _string_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:25
msgid ""
"Names are used in [attribute sets](./syntax.md#attrs-literal), [`let` "
"bindings](./syntax.md#let-expressions), and [`inherit`](./"
"syntax.md#inheriting-attributes). Two names are the same if they represent "
"the same sequence of characters, regardless of whether they are written as "
"identifiers or strings."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:28
msgid "Keywords"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:30
msgid ""
"These keywords are reserved and cannot be used as [identifiers]"
"(#identifiers):"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:32
msgid "[`assert`](./syntax.md#assertions)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:33
msgid "[`else`](./syntax.md#conditionals)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:34
msgid "[`if`](./syntax.md#conditionals)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:35
msgid "[`in`](./syntax.md#let-expressions)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:36
msgid "[`inherit`](./syntax.md#inheriting-attributes)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:37
msgid "[`let`](./syntax.md#let-expressions)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:38
msgid "[`or`](./operators.md#attribute-selection) (see note)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:39
msgid "[`rec`](./syntax.md#recursive-sets)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:40
msgid "[`then`](./syntax.md#conditionals)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:41
msgid "[`with`](./syntax.md#with-expressions)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:46
msgid "**Note**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:48
msgid ""
"The Nix language evaluator currently allows `or` to be used as a name in "
"some contexts, for backwards compatibility reasons. Users are advised not to "
"rely on this."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/identifiers.md:51
msgid ""
"There are long-standing issues with how `or` is parsed as a name, which "
"can't be resolved without making a breaking change to the language."
msgstr ""
